==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Alternative forms===
* [[Maffia]] {{qualifier|less common}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|it|en}}. Perhaps from {{etyl|it|en}} {{term|mafia||spirit of hostility to the law|lang=it}} or from {{etyl|scn|en}} {{term|mafia||boldness, bravado|lang=scn}}. See [[w:Mafia|the Wikipedia article]] for more discussion of the origin of the word.

===Pronunciation===
{{a|US}} {{IPA|/ˈmɑː.f.i.ə/|lang=en}}
{{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈmæf.i.ə/|lang=en}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun|head=the Mafia}}

# {{context|specifically|lang=en}} An international [[criminal]] organization of [[Sicilian]] origin operating in [[Italy]] and the [[United States]].
# {{context|by extension|lang=en}} Any organized crime [[syndicate]] operating internationally in high-level [[organized crime]]; {{non-gloss definition|often with a modifying adjective, such as a nationality}}.
#: ''Somehow he managed to upset the Russian '''Mafia'''.''
# A [[party game]] modelling a [[conflict]] between an informed [[minority]] (the mafia) and an uninformed [[majority]] (the innocents). Each player is secretly assigned a role within one of these teams, and the innocents attempt to identify the mafia members before they are all "murdered".
# {{alternative case form of|mafia|nodot=1}} {{qualifier|an entity which attempts to control a specified arena}}.

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|organization of Sicilian origin}} [[Cosa Nostra]], [[mob]]
* {{sense|any organized crime syndicate}} [[mob]]

